verification effort has started, but is not yet complete.
• Not_Started: The verification effort has not yet started.
• Done: The verification effort is complete.
This conditional result is determined by examining the average coverage score and the
state of the number of tests and the number of failing tests. For example, to consider
a feature to be In_Progress, there must be at least one test written and at least one
coverage object hit. However, to consider a feature to be Done, there must be no failing
tests and all coverage must be hit.
Defining the Result Value in an HVP Language
VCS Coverage only allows you to define the result value in a plan. You cannot define it in
a feature.
The result value is calculated after the scores are propagated. It is calculated in each plan/
feature scope but not in a measure, source, or region level. When the definition of a top
plan is different from a subplan, an error is issued. The result value is same as enum value.
Following is an example HVP plan with the result value defined:
Example 1 HVP Plan With Result Value Defined
plan plan_top;
result overall_status;
value.Not_started = default;
value.In_Progress = ((Line <= 0.6) || (Toggle <= 0.7));

Defining Conditional Results in Verification Planner
value.Done = ((Line >= 0.95) && (Toggle >= 0.9));

feature F1;
measure Line, Cond, FSM, Toggle, Branch Measure_1;
source = "module : tb";

feature F2;
measure Line, Cond, FSM, Toggle, Branch Measure_1;
source = "module: counter", "tree: tb.ff";

feature F2_sub;
measure Line, Toggle, Cond Measure_1;
source = "tree: tb.cnt";
