Example 73 Assert function inside always_comb
always_comb begin : AL
assert final (0); //No Label
end
Example 74 for-loop statement is inside always_comb
always_comb begin // Not Named
for(int i=0;i<1;i++)
A1: assert final (0);
end
Example 75 for-loop statement is inside initial
initial begin : INI // Behavioral
for(int i=0;i<1;i++)
A1: assert final (0);
end
• XPROP is not supported.
• VCS does not support signature-based control for immediate assertion which is defined
inside the function body or for loop.
Example 76 Assertion Defined Inside the Function Body
reg a, b, c, d;
function f(input a, b);
L_simple: assert (a > b);
#1;
begin:block1
f(a, b);
end
begin:block2
f(a, b);
end
end

Enabling Fail-Only Feature
where filename can be any user defined ASCII file. The <filename> contains the list of
assertions to be moved to fail-only mode.
You can specify the module name and assertion name that you want to move to fail-only
mode in a <filename>.
Following is the format to specify assertions in the text file:
<modulename> <assertion name>
For the assertions which are used in named scope, the relative hierarchical path must be
specified. For example, if you have an assertion A1 defined inside named always block as
shown below:
always@(posedge clk) begin: ALWYS
A1: assert property (a && b |-> ##1 out);
The configuration file must be as follows:
top ALWYS.A1
Example 78 test.v
bit a,b,c,d,e;
bit clk;
mod1 m1(clk,a,b,c);
mod2 m2(clk, d, e);
always
#1 clk = ~clk;
a = 1; b=0; c=0; d = 1; e = 0;
#100 b = 1; e = 1;
#20 $finish;
end
module mod1(input clk, input a, input b,input c);
A1: assert property( @(posedge clk) a ## [1:$] b |-> c);
module mod2(input clk, input d, input e);
A2: cover property(@(posedge clk) d ##[0:$] e);

class c;
static bit a;
function setA(input in);
a = in;

static function getA;
static reg a;

return a;

c c1 = new;

always #1 clk = ~clk;
ASTR: assert property (@(posedge clk) (str == "abc"));//
ADYNQSIZE: assert property (@(posedge clk) dynQ.size());//
ADYNARRSIZE: assert property (@(posedge clk) dynArr.size()); //
ADYNARRVAL: assert property (@(posedge clk) dynArr[2]); //
clk = 0;
dynQ[0] = 1;
c1.setA(0);
dynArr[0] = 1;

#10 dynQ[1] = 1;
dynArr[1] = 1;
#10 dynQ[2] = 1;
dynArr[2] = 1;
#10 dynQ[3] = 1;
dynArr[3] = 1;
c1.setA(1);
#10 dynQ[4] = 1;
dynArr[4] = 1;
#10 dynQ[5] = 1;
dynArr[5] = 1;
#10 dynQ.pop_front();
#10 dynQ.pop_front();
#10 dynQ.pop_front();
#10 str = "abc";
#20 $finish;
end
