Improved MSV Parameter Override and Optimizations in Verilog-AMS Flow
The parameter vsup of capacitor instance BOT1 has the most common value (1.1) in
module mid.
For the three capacitor instances (top.m1.BOT1, top.m2.BOT1, and top.m3.BOT1),
an optimization is used. The less commonly used parameter value of 2.8 for instance
top.m3.BOT1 is passed using the hierarchical format (explicit assignment), whereas
the more frequently used value of 1.1 for the other two instances (top.m1.BOT1, and
top.m2.BOT1) is passed using the folded format (implicit assignment).
Improved Partitioning for SPICE Primitive and Sub-Circuit
Parameter Values
To optimize partitioning efficiency, VCS handles boundary SPICE parameters using two
distinct methods:
• Folded Format: The most common value of a boundary Spice parameter is passed in a
folded manner through a partition file.
• Flattened Format: Parameter values for all other scenarios are partitioned in a flattened
hierarchical format via a separate partition file.
To enable this feature, use the -adopt sp_param_part_enh compile option.
Consider the following testcases:
