Improving Compile Time in the Partition Compile Flow
• This feature is not supported for VHDL designs.
• FSMs found in nested structures are only supported when any array of structures is
at the innermost level. Thus, the example below is not supported for FSM monitoring,
because there is an array of structures at the top level instead of the innermost one.
struct {
struct {
logic[1:0] cur_st, nxt_st;
}inner;
}slot[2]
Improving Compile Time in the Partition Compile Flow
You may instruct VCS to dump a folded view of a design instead of its elaborated view
during compilation in a partition compile flow. If the total number of instances in a design
is very large and its hierarchical depth is relatively small, the -cm_instr folded_design
switch enables you to improve compile-time performance for the design.
The syntax of the -cm_instr folded_design compile-time switch is as follows:
vcs -cm line+tgl -cm_instr folded_design
