Support for Net with Data Types
VCS supports net declaration with explicit data types as defined in the SystemVerilog
LRM.
The data type of a net can be any one of the following:
• A 4-state integral type, including a packed array or a packed structure.
• A fixed-size unpacked array or unpacked structure, where each element has a valid
data type for a net.
You can use any 4-state data type to declare a net.
VCS also supports declaration of explicit port kind. Port kind can be any of the net type
keywords or the keyword var. If you omit the keywords during port declaration, the port
kind is determined as per rules specified in the IEEE SystemVerilog LRM Std 1800-2012
Section 23.2.2.3.
VCS supports port kind in both ANSI and non-ANSI mode. In case of ANSI declaration,
rules are applied as per rules specified in the IEEE SystemVerilog LRM Std 1800-2012
Section 23.2.2.3. In case of non-ANSI declaration, net or variable declaration is complete
in itself and does not depend upon the I/O declaration that comes before or after the type
declaration.
