Support for Modeling Isolation Cell Without Enable Pin in Liberty
VCS NLP supports modeling of an isolation cell without enable pin in the Liberty file. With
this enhancement, VCS NLP can insert isolation cells without an enable signal pin.
Figure 91 Isolation Cell Without Enable Pin

Support for Modeling Isolation Cell Without Enable Pin in Liberty
You must use the -isolation_signal option with empty braces (-isolation_signal {})
to specify the tool to infer isolation cells with no enable pin.
set_isolation IS01 -dmain PD1 -clamp_value latch -applies_to outputs \
-location self -isolation_supply_set [TOP_prim} \
- isolation_signal {}
It is an error to specify the -isolation_sense option in an isolation strategy while using
-isolation_signal {} .
The following sample liberty file shows how dual-rail isolation cell with no enable pin is
modeled in the Liberty:
Example 120 Liberty File
library (mylib) {
…
voltage_map(DVDD, 0.8);
voltage_map(DVDDB, 0.8);
…
/* Signal pins D(data) is powered by DVDD(primary_power) while output
signal Z is powered by DVDDB(backup_power) hence this is an Isolation
Cell*/
cell(Isolation_Cell_no_enable_signal_pin) {
is_isolation_cell : true;
pg_pin(DVDD) {
voltage_name : DVDD;
pg_type : primary_power;
}
pg_pin(DVDDB) {
voltage_name : DVDDB;
pg_type : backup_power;
}
pg_pin(VSS) {
voltage_name : VSS;
pg_type : primary_ground;
}
pin(D) {
direction : input;
related_power_pin : DVDD;
related_ground_pin : VSS;
isolation_cell_data_pin : true;
}
pin(Z) {
direction : output;
related_power_pin : DVDDB;
related_ground_pin : VSS;
function : "D";
clamp_latch_function : "!DVDD";
power_down_function : "!DVDDB + VSS";

