Support for Overriding Design Connection With UPF Connection
on a Power Switch Acknowledgment Signal
The acknowledgment port (defined using -ack_port option) of a power switch shows
the status of power switch (defined using create_power_switch command) during
The power switch drives its acknowledgment port. However, in some cases, HDL driver
also drives the acknowledgment port, creating a multi-driver scenario. By default, VCS
NLP issues a warning message for a multi-driver scenario if it is a valid Verilog scenario,
otherwise it issues an error message.
You can use the -power=disable_ack_design_driver option at compile time to disable
the HDL drivers (if any) of an acknowledgment port and only keep the power-switch driver.

