-dir

Use <dir> as the directory for source data.
-sdb

Generate a compressed csv database in the directory <dir> for Verdi.
-merge

Create a merged database in the directory <dir>.
-purge

Purge variables from the database specified in <file>.
-purgeX

Purge variables from the database excluding those specified in <file>.
-elfile

Exclude the specified bins in <file> from the report.
-exclude

Specify bin category to exclude bin specified in elfile (Default: uncovered).
-work

Specify work <dir> (Default: WORK).
-wdiv

Computes weighted diversity.
-zip

Specify compression <level> 0-9 (Default: 0).
-purge_untag

Purge untagged biased or scope variables.
-base_merge

Specify the base class merge <level> >= 1.
-diff

Diff two directories and annotate the report of the first directory.
-show

Show test names or record locations. (Default: records).
-illegal_attr

Annotate illegal attributes from RCA information.
-illegal_group

Group illegal RCA information.
-rca_effort_attr

Annotate RCA effort attributes for bins with no RCA information.
-part_select

Include part selects of variables in the report.
-sbin_merge

Group illegal RCA information.
-rca_effort_attr

Annotate RCA effort attributes for bins with no RCA information.
-part_select

Include part selects of variables in the report.
-sbin_merge

Specify merge operation for custom bins. (Default: reuse+add).
-purge_sbin

Purge sbins of variables from the database specified in <file>.
-purgeX_sbin

Purge sbins of variables from the database excluding those specified in <file>.
-purge_key

Purge variables from the database as per <key> uvm+rca+sbin.
-purgeX_key

Purge variables from the database excluding those specified as per <key> uvm+rca
+sbin.

The following is the crg command to convert a cdb database to a single compressed csv
file (SDB file) in Verdi ICO:
% crg -dir <cdb file> -sdb <sdb file> -illegal_attr -illegal_group
